      "content_preview": "**What is Fourier Transform ?** Like RGB color mixer where adding 1 color created a new color. Fourier Transform are exactly like that but for Wave and in reverse. You decompose 1 wave into 3 fundamental waves, these 3 waves can basically form any type of waves form you can imagine.  \n\n![[Pasted image 20260204173815.png | 333]]\nimage source: https://nautil.us/the-math-trick-behind-mp3s-jpegs-and-homer-simpsons-face-234629/\n\n\nWhat is a Transform ? **mapping between value Domains.** + ? (like con Lợn -> con Heo, while both describe the exact same thing, just different expression)\n![[Pasted image 20251217031845.png]]\n\n**Sinusoids** is great bc its the only **Wave form that doesn't change shape when subjected to a *Linear Time System (LTI)***\nNote: doensn't mean it easier to work with.\n![[Pasted image 20251217032203.png]]\n\nThink in term of gain/amplitude and change in phase through a system at any given frequency. \n![[Pasted image 20251217032542.png]]\n\n![[Pasted image 20251217032916.png]]\n\n![[Pasted image 20251217033135.png]]\n\n![[Pasted image 20251217033211.png]]\n\n![[Pasted image 20251217033245.png]]\n\n"
